[
    {
        "content": "<p>I had a proof which worked but then after updating mathlib (I think the mathlib version I worked with was only a few weeks older) the <code>rw</code> tactic fails to find the pattern even after explicitly specifying all the arguments (see the last <code>rw</code> in the proof of the last theorem):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Star</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Analysis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">InnerProductSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Calculus</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Analysis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">SpecialFunctions</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Trigonometric</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Deriv</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CompleteField</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">StarOrdered</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">MeasureTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Integral</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IntervalIntegral</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FundThmCalculus</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">BourbakiWitt</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PlaneCurve</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Curvature for plane curves. This is usually called just the curvature function of a plane curve</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">in most elementary differential geometry texts, but because this definition is slightly different</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">from the general definition of the curvature function of a general parametrized curve (which is</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">always non-negative and only expresses magnitude as opposed to this definition which can also be</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">negative and expresses also direction) we call this the oriented curvature, this is also the name</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">given in the Wikipedia article about curvature in the section about plane curves. This definition is</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">meaningful only for regular plane curves which are twice continuously differentiable on an</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">interval I. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">orientedCurvature</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iteratedDeriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">!!</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">det</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">‖^</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Normal vector at a point of a plane curve. This definition is only meaningful when c is</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">differentiable at t, and it's supposed to be used for plane curves parametrized by arc-length.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">normal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">!₂</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- A simpler formula for the curvature of a plane curve parametrized by arc-length, or in other</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">words with unit speed. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">orientedCurvature_of_unit_speed_curve</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">OrdConnected</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">orientedCurvature</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inner</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">iteratedDeriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">normal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">orientedCurvature</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">normal</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inner_eq_star_dotProduct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">iteratedDeriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">!₂</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofLp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofLp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">]]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sub_eq_neg_add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofLp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">iteratedDeriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofLp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">deriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofLp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">iteratedDeriv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofLp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 579576701,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Novak",
        "timestamp": 1773610294
    },
    {
        "content": "<ol>\n<li>Which version are you on?</li>\n<li>Does <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false</code> fix it?</li>\n</ol>",
        "id": 579576864,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773610469
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think I use the latest version because the issue also exists in the web editor with the latest mathlib version.</p>",
        "id": 579577002,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Novak",
        "timestamp": 1773610653
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If 2 does fix the problem, you can refer to <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113486-General-announcements/topic/releases.20of.20new.20Lean.20versions/near/574617729\">#General announcements &gt; releases of new Lean versions @ 💬</a> for more information, and follow <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113488\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/backward.2EisDefEq.2ErespectTransparency/with/579473923\">#general &gt; backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency</a>  for more progress on fixing these</p>",
        "id": 579577004,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773610657
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah this also applies to the latest web editor version</p>",
        "id": 579577027,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773610681
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Where do I need to put this line?</p>",
        "id": 579577051,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Novak",
        "timestamp": 1773610703
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can either put it at the start of the file, or put <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false in</code> before each <code>def</code>/<code>theorem</code></p>",
        "id": 579577122,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773610781
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you feel like helping with fixing this, you can also put <code>#defeq_abuse in</code> before the theorem and see if the diagnoses matches any reports in <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113488\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/backward.2EisDefEq.2ErespectTransparency/with/579473923\">#general &gt; backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency</a> , and report it if it is not there yet</p>",
        "id": 579577228,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773610902
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873350\">Weiyi Wang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/rw.20fails.20to.20find.20pattern.20after.20updating.20mathlib/near/579577122\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You can either put it at the start of the file, or put <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false in</code> before each <code>def</code>/<code>theorem</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>When I put it at the begging of the file I get an error on the first import, but if I put it after the imports, then it indeed solves the problem</p>",
        "id": 579577301,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Novak",
        "timestamp": 1773610971
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah sorry, yeah it should be after imports</p>",
        "id": 579577313,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773610988
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873350\">Weiyi Wang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/rw.20fails.20to.20find.20pattern.20after.20updating.20mathlib/near/579577313\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ah sorry, yeah it should be after imports</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Oh, o.k. Thank you very much.</p>",
        "id": 579577368,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Novak",
        "timestamp": 1773611057
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873350\">Weiyi Wang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/rw.20fails.20to.20find.20pattern.20after.20updating.20mathlib/near/579577228\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>#defeq_abuse in</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I put the <code>#defeq_abuse in</code> command before the theorem and got some output, which I don't fully understand. Should I send it to thread you linked?</p>",
        "id": 579577703,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Novak",
        "timestamp": 1773611446
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And is it acceptable to have the <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false</code> line in a file that I want to contribute to Mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 579577956,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Novak",
        "timestamp": 1773611726
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>I put the <code>#defeq_abuse in</code> command before the theorem and got some output, which I don't fully understand. Should I send it to thread you linked?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think it doesn't harm to send it there</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And is it acceptable to have the <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false</code> line in a file that I want to contribute to Mathlib?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The current standard in Mathlib seems to be \"feel free to put it before any theorem, but don't put it at the beginning of a file\"</p>",
        "id": 579578003,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773611805
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>O.k, thank you very much!</p>",
